Many people have sent us mail regarding PC NetHack, expressing the
same concerns.  Izchak suggested i post a message telling everyone
what the current situation is.

And now, the state of PC NetHack 3.0f (patchlevel 2) address...

	PC NetHack can now compile without TERMLIB if ANSI_DEFAULT is
	used, saving about 2K of executable size with Turbo C.  This
	obviates the need for Fish's termcap library.

	Various compile errors have been fixed.  The bflush() in
	bones.c was enclosed in #ifdef ZEROCOMP, the chdirx()
	prototype has been corrected, &c.

	The "At gets null" and "Really save?" bugs have been fixed.

	If IBM_BIOS is set, it will auto-detect the dimensions of the
	screen.

	The color strings have been generalized into an array.
	Objects now come in 3 colors: organic green (food, potions),
	metallic cyan (weapons, armor, ...), and leftover magenta.
	Fountains are blue.  Also, MSDOSCOLOR has been generalized
	into TEXTCOLOR, so that System V r3.2 unix systems can use the
	terminfo color sequences.

	The shift-direction bug with number_pad on is being investigated.

	Makefile.pc has been replaced with a tested, working Makefile
	that Paul Gyugyi sent us.

	Timo Hakulinen sent us patches porting NetHack to OS/2.  They
	have been incorporated.

The Patch2 distribution is currently planned for release Tuesday.

I intend to send comp.binaries.ibm.pc PC NetHack 3.0f after the Patch2
release.  It should be worth waiting for.

-3.


